# Traductor Auth Server

## Overview
Self-hosted Better Auth server for Traductor Desktop and other applications.
Production URL: https://auth.niklauss.uk
Uses Hexagonal Architecture (Ports & Adapters) for easy infrastructure swapping.

## Tech Stack
- Node.js 20 + TypeScript (ESM, NodeNext)
- Hono (web framework)
- Better Auth (authentication)
- Prisma + Neon PostgreSQL
- Upstash Redis

## Critical: ESM Imports
MUST use `.js` extension for relative imports:
```typescript
import { auth } from './lib/auth.js';  // CORRECT
import { auth } from './lib/auth';     // WRONG
```

## Project Structure
```
src/
├── index.ts           # Server entry point
├── core/              # Hexagonal architecture
│   ├── ports/         # Interfaces
│   └── container.ts   # Dependency injection
├── adapters/          # Port implementations
│   ├── database/      # Prisma adapter
│   ├── cache/         # Upstash/Redis adapters
│   └── config/        # Env adapter
├── lib/
│   ├── auth.ts        # Better Auth config
│   ├── redis.ts       # Upstash Redis client
│   └── tokens.ts      # JWT token service
└── routes/
    ├── auth.ts        # /api/auth/*
    ├── tokens.ts      # /api/tokens/*
    └── usage.ts       # /api/usage/*
```

## Integrating New Apps
1. Add origin to `TRUSTED_ORIGINS` in server `.env`
2. Restart container: `sudo docker restart traductor-auth`
3. Client-side:
```typescript
import { createAuthClient } from 'better-auth/client';
const authClient = createAuthClient({ baseURL: 'https://auth.niklauss.uk' });
```

## API Endpoints
- POST /api/auth/sign-up - Register
- POST /api/auth/sign-in/email - Login
- POST /api/auth/sign-out - Logout
- GET /api/auth/session - Current session
- POST /api/tokens/ephemeral - Generate JWT (1h)
- POST /api/tokens/verify - Verify token
- GET /api/usage - Usage stats
- GET /health - Health check

## Commands
```bash
npm run dev          # Development
npm run build        # Build TypeScript
npx prisma studio    # Database GUI
npx prisma db push   # Sync schema
```

## Production (AWS EC2)
```bash
ssh -i "traductor-auth-key.pem" ec2-user@54.90.128.44
sudo docker logs traductor-auth
sudo docker restart traductor-auth
```

## Code Style
- Strict TypeScript
- Async/await over promises
- Structured error responses
- Zod for validation
- Never log plain tokens

## Key Files
1. src/index.ts - Read first
2. src/lib/auth.ts - Better Auth config
3. prisma/schema.prisma - Database schema
4. Dockerfile - Production build
